 ### Addendum: effort setting

 The live tests on `claude-sonnet-5-5` with `ExtendedThinking::Adaptive` failed 3 of 6, because turn 1 had no thinking block. This model has the default effort `medium`, and at `medium` it can skip thinking on a short task. Sven chose to add an `effort` builder option (`Effort`) in this PR. The default sends no effort. With `Effort::High` the live tests failed again. A later probe (6 requests, no streaming, the same request as the crate) showed the cause: at `high` the model did not think in 3 of 3 plain requests. At `max` it thought. The earlier probes got thinking because their prompt started with the redacted-thinking trigger string. On `claude-sonnet-5-5` this string gives a normal `thinking` block with empty text, not a `redacted_thinking` block. The stream parser is not the cause: the same request without streaming also had no thinking block. Rulings: the Adaptive live tests use `Effort::Max`, and the redacted live test runs on the Enabled path (`claude-haiku-4-5`). This addendum replaces the non-goal above that excludes an effort setting.
